# Update Architecture Document When Needed

When acting as architect, tech lead, or when making or reviewing **architectural** changes, keep the System Architecture Specification in sync.

**Document:** `docs/SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE_SPECIFICATION.md`

**Update the doc when:**
- Adding or removing runtime components (APIs, workers, schedulers, new entry points)
- Changing technical stack (frameworks, DB, cache, auth, messaging, build/deploy)
- Restructuring modules, layers, or dependencies (folder/solution/project changes)
- Changing domain model, data layer, or major execution flows
- Changing configuration, deployment, or environment handling in a way that affects the spec

**How to update:**
- Edit the relevant section(s) only; keep the same structure and factual, discovery-only style
- Do not add opinions, risks, or recommendations—only what the system **is** and **how it works**
- If a new flow is significant, add it under "Execution flows"; if an existing flow changes, update that bullet

**When not to update:**
- Bug fixes, refactors, or feature work that do not change architecture, topology, or documented behavior
- Cosmetic or copy edits that don’t affect accuracy
